<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

        <title>About [[title]]</title>

        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/styles.css">
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/about.css">
    </head>
    <body>
        <%view navbar %>
        <div id="main-content">
            <div id="about-title-text">About [[title]]</div>
            <hr>
            <div id="about-text">
                [[title]] is an open-source video platform that is inspired by the old web.
                It encourages original and creative content instead of blind repetition.
                [[title]] also supports many resolutions, although 640x480 is highly popular because it looks nice.
                Since [[title]] uses barley any javascript, you can also run it on old browsers, or environments where JavaScript maybe not be available (e. g. Tor Browser).
                You will only need javascript when uploading videos, and there is an optional javascript on the watch page if you want to use keyboard shortcuts.
            </div>
        </div>
        <%view footer %>
    </body>
</html>
